> FITTING CN UNITS FASTER:
> Starting with aroma.affymetrix v0.9.5 you can fit all CN units/probes
> much much faster by:

> only the SNP units have to be fitted.  The above will probably bring
> down the processing time to half of what you have now.

Thanks for the advice, I've done that and the analysis of CN probes
only took 3 hours! Now I'm back to fitting SNP probes and the ETA is
down to:
20081204 10:24:24|  Started: 20081203 22:51:08
20081204 10:24:24|  Estimated time left: 14260.7min
20081204 10:24:24|  ETA: 20081214 08:05:08

This is way better, but still, the difference between CN probes and
SNP probes is so huge!

> PROCESSING DATA IN PARALLEL:
> As argued in other threads, parts of the CRMA method are single array
> by nature (especially with AvgCnPlm) and the upcoming CRMA v2 will be
> truly a single-array method.  This means that you can process subsets
> of your data set in parallel on multiple machines and then combine
> them at the end of the pipeline.  Currently this has to be done
> manually.  Here is an example illustrating how it could be done
> (though, I haven't had time to verify it):

This is actually very cool stuff, and while I'm really looking forward
to using CRMA v2, I will try your suggestions for parallelizing the
analysis in the next couple weeks. I'll tell you how it goes. I just
hope you don't release CRMA v2 before I finish! :)

> PS. FYI, the release of the truly single-array CRMA v2 method is
> getting closer (it is beta tested by collaborators).  This will allow
> you process also the FLN step in parallel.  It also includes a
> (single-array) probe-position normalization following the crosstalk
> calibration, which improves the SNR of the final CN estimates even
> further.  DS.

This sounds great. Do you have an idea of when CRMA v2 will be ready
for prime time?

Thanks a lot,
    Nico

