On Thu, Dec 4, 2008 at 12:20 PM, Henrik Bengtsson <h...@stat.berkeley.edu> wrote:
> Hi,
>
> wow this turns out to be a never ending story ;)  So, this time it is
> actually a problem with the affxparser package and the Affymetrix
> Fusion SDK library it uses.
>
> If you look at the output of print(cdf) or getChipType(cdf) you'll
> find that the chip type reported is wrong - it contains a full path
> with slashes.  The chip type of a CDF is inferred "virtually" from the
> CDF header, which we get by called readCdfHeader() of affxparser.
> When I look back at your earlier replies and put things together, I
> notice that you get the following:
>
> cdf <- AffymetrixCdfFile$byChipType("MoGene-1_0-st-v1", tags="r3");
> pathname <- getPathname(cdf);
> print(pathname);
>
> [1] "\\RES2K3FS01/RESAffymetrix/ANNOTATION/aromaAffymetrix/annotationData/chipTypes/MoGene-1_0-st-v1/MoGene-1_0-st-v1,r3.cdf"
>
> hdr <- readCdfHeader(pathname);
> str(hdr);
>
> List of 12
>  $ ncols      : int 1050
>  $ nrows      : int 1050
>  $ nunits     : int 35512
>  $ nqcunits   : int 1
>  $ refseq     : chr ""
>  $ chiptype   : chr "RES2K3FS01/RESAffymetrix/ANNOTATION/
> aromaAffymetrix/annotationData/chipTypes/MoGene-1_0-st-v1/MoGene-1_0-
> st-v1,r3"
>  $ filename   : chr "\\\\RES2K3FS01/RESAffymetrix/ANNOTATION/
> aromaAffymetrix/annotationData/chipTypes/MoGene-1_0-st-v1/MoGene-1_0-
> st-v1,r3.cdf"
>  $ rows       : int 1050
>  $ cols       : int 1050
>  $ probesets  : int 35512
>  $ qcprobesets: int 1
>  $ reference  : chr ""
>
> NOTE the 'chipType' element.  It is reported as a long path, not just
> the last part 'MoGene-1_0-st-v1,r3'.  The thing is that in a CDF file
> there exist no specification of a chip type - the file format does not
> contain that - instead the chip type is inferred from the pathname.
> Somehow does the Fusion SDK library, which affxparser is using, fail
> to extract the filename, i.e. fail to drop the path from the full
> pathname.  It is likely that the backslashes at the beginning cause
> this problem.
>
> As a workaround for now, because I think it will be a while before
> this is fixed in Fusion SDK, I now have filePath() to always return
> forward slashes for network paths.  See if the following solves the
> problem:
>
> library("aroma.affymetrix");
> source("http://www.braju.com/R/patches/R.utils/20081204/filePath.R");
>
> If it does, I'll update R.utils again.
>
> Cheers
>
> Henrik
>
