> I just ran an analysis of 44 controls with the  5.0 platform. And I
> ran everything from the tutorial:
>
> http://groups.google.com/group/aroma-affymetrix/web/total-copy-number-analysis-6-0
>
> And the script ran perfectly
>
> But when I read the regions.xls I realized that no "call" column was
> displayed. I  understood that the call column has the state of the
> region: neutral, gain or  loss.
>
> Did I miss something? Or should I do something else?

That vignette is using the CbsModel, which segments data using the
Circular Binary Segmentation (CBS) model, which algorithm is
implemented in the DNAcopy package.  The CBS algorithm does *not* call
copy-number states.  For further details, see the help of DNAcopy
package and the CBS papers.

You might think of the GLAD segmentation method fitted by GladModel.
That calls the state of the regions.  However, you will probably find
that too slow for processing the GWS6 chip types.

Hope this helps

/Henrik

